<http://data.silknow.org/object/929b3134-a623-3de4-b6d8-d5e987ddd9f0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A pair of women's shoes made of silk., woven in Iran, in a pattern of ornate apricot-coloure flowers and abstract curvilinear shapes in white and green, all surrounded with borders of flowers against a black ground. The quarters and tongue are edged with two strands of narrow metal lace (braid).\n\nThe shoes each have a leather sole and white leather rand.  They have pointed toes curving upwards and shaped wooden heels."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/929b3134-a623-3de4-b6d8-d5e987ddd9f0> .

